      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "(g) Act for, on behalf of and at the direction of the Mayor in the exercise of all functions, powers and duties which the Mayor may have pursuant to the New York City Seasonal Financing Act of 1975, Public Law 94-143, as the same may be from time to time amended, and a credit agreement made thereunder as of December 30, 1975 by and among the United States of America on the one hand and the State of New York, the City of New York and the New York State Emergency Financial Control Board on the other hand, including, but not limited to, full power to execute for, on behalf of, and at the direction of the Mayor, any document pursuant to such agreement and any agreement, amendment to agreement or other document pursuant to such law; and to act for, on behalf of and at the direction of the Mayor in the exercise of all functions, powers and duties which the Mayor may have pursuant to the New York City Loan Guarantee Act of 1978, P. L. 95-339, as the same may be from time to time amended, an Agreement to Guarantee by and among the United State of America, the State of New York, The City of New York, the New York State Financial Control Board and the Municipal Assistance Corporation for The City of New York, a Loan Agreement between the City of New York and certain banks, and pension funds, and a Guranteed Bond Purchase Agreement by and among The City of New York, certain City pension funds, certain State pension funds and the United States of America, each dated as of November 15, 1978, including, but not limited to, full power to execute for, on behalf of, and at the direction of the Mayor, any document pursuant to any such agreement and any agreement, amendment to agreement or other document pursuant to such law. The exercise of functions, powers and duties for, on behalf of and at the direction of the Mayor by such Deputy Mayor pursuant to this delegation shall not require the consent in writing of the Mayor or any other official of the City.",
